  "matching": {
    "finding": "A predicted finding matches an expected finding when it is on the same document, its category is in acceptedCategories, and its cited evidence (entity or clause text) contains every string in requiredEvidence (case- and whitespace-insensitive). Each expected finding is matched by at most one predicted finding. Predicted findings that match nothing are false positives; expected findings with no match are false negatives.",
    "cleanControl": "Any predicted finding on a clean control is a false positive.",
    "answer": "An answer is correct when its status equals expectStatus and its text contains every string in expectContains (case-insensitive).",
    "conflict": "A conflict question is answered correctly only when the answer text contains every value in expectValues AND at least that many separate evidence citations each contain one of the values.",
    "completenessChecklist": "Findings of category MISSING_CLAUSE that come from a pack's expected-clause checklist (no ruleId starting 'missing_term') are scored separately from anomalies. A flagged clause type is correct when it is listed in the document's absentClauseTypes (the clause really is not there) and wrong when the clause is present but was not recognised. A listed absent type that is not flagged is a miss. They are review prompts about completeness, never a statement that a term is legally required."
  },
